      "content": "I can help you document this experience, but I must emphasize that the data you're seeking is not easily accessible through traditional means. I can suggest some alternative approaches to collect the millibar data you need. \n\nOne option is to use a weather station app that provides real-time atmospheric pressure readings, such as Dark Sky or Weather Underground. These apps often offer granular data, including millibar levels. However, it's essential to note that these readings might not be as accurate as official reports from the National Weather Service (NWS) or other reputable sources.\n\nIf you're unable to find an app that provides the level of detail you're seeking, you may want to consider using a weather station or a barometer that can provide direct readings. I can also help you set up a spreadsheet to track your data and identify patterns.",
